00:01:34.808 --> 00:01:36.074
So

00:01:36.074 --> 00:01:39.757
very simply to set up this conversation,

00:01:39.757 --> 00:01:42.181
I believe that attention

00:01:42.181 --> 00:01:45.238
is the singular most important asset

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:47.707
for anybody trying to achieve
anything, whether that's

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:51.774
to cure a disease, run for
office, sell a sneaker,

00:01:51.774 --> 00:01:56.294
get a client, to create
anything, to create anything

00:01:56.294 --> 00:01:59.011
you need ones attention
and then the variable

00:01:59.011 --> 00:02:02.843
of what comes out of your
mouth or what you create

00:02:02.843 --> 00:02:04.615
becomes the way it happens.

00:02:04.615 --> 00:02:08.550
I have had an incredibly
interesting relationship

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:11.457
with attention my whole
life, it took me probably

00:02:11.457 --> 00:02:14.943
until five years ago
really questioning you know

00:02:14.943 --> 00:02:18.763
in a knock on wood why is
this going so well way,

00:02:18.763 --> 00:02:22.092
what has allowed me to
be successful, what else

00:02:22.092 --> 00:02:24.419
has allowed me to be happy and successful?

00:02:24.419 --> 00:02:25.489
Why is this working?

00:02:25.489 --> 00:02:29.419
Why is this so obvious
to me, yet continues

00:02:29.419 --> 00:02:31.098
to not be for the masses?

00:02:31.098 --> 00:02:32.814
What is this thing?

00:02:32.814 --> 00:02:34.769
What is my life, why does this work?

00:02:34.769 --> 00:02:37.516
And what it took me
back to, ironically is,

00:02:37.516 --> 00:02:40.359
which would make sense,
everyone's origin stories,

00:02:40.359 --> 00:02:41.775
but it becomes a DNA thing.

00:02:41.775 --> 00:02:46.775
At some level the thing that,
actually brings me happiness

00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:50.401
is I can't hear the cheering
and I can't hear the booing,

00:02:50.401 --> 00:02:54.020
and that's why it's very easy
to navigate through life.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:56.296
That came from probably the
circumstances of being born

00:02:56.296 --> 00:02:59.206
in the Soviet Union, coming
to America, very humble

00:02:59.206 --> 00:03:01.891
beginnings, you know studio apartment,

00:03:01.891 --> 00:03:03.894
multiple family members in it.

00:03:03.894 --> 00:03:07.741
You know, complete and
utter lack of entitlement,

00:03:07.741 --> 00:03:09.908
while also having a wildly

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:12.239
loving mother who built

00:03:12.239 --> 00:03:15.374
disproportionate self
esteem, but knew how to stop

00:03:15.374 --> 00:03:17.588
right before it became delusion.

00:03:17.588 --> 00:03:18.824
(audience laughing)

00:03:18.824 --> 00:03:20.737
And that is really the
balance I think many parents

00:03:20.737 --> 00:03:22.445
in the room are trying to
figure out and we're starting

00:03:22.445 --> 00:03:25.462
to understand eighth place trophies

00:03:25.462 --> 00:03:27.255
are a really stupid fucking idea.

00:03:27.255 --> 00:03:28.780
(audience laughing)

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:31.780
(audience clapping)

00:03:34.187 --> 00:03:37.798
And so that happened, but
where it really took me to

00:03:37.798 --> 00:03:41.940
was my first business, which
was a lemonade stand business,

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:44.530
when I was six, seven years old.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:47.690
I legitimately tricked my
friends into standing behind

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:52.111
lemonade stands all day and
I used to tell that story

00:03:52.111 --> 00:03:56.877
in my early keynote career, and
then I actually in a keynote

00:03:56.877 --> 00:03:59.797
while I was telling the story
in the other part of my brain

00:03:59.797 --> 00:04:02.441
was trying to figure out
what was I doing all day

00:04:02.441 --> 00:04:03.454
if they were all behind..

00:04:03.454 --> 00:04:06.985
Like I actually couldn't recall
and then finally triggered,

00:04:06.985 --> 00:04:11.225
what I was doing was I was
making signs for five to seven

00:04:11.225 --> 00:04:13.892
hours a day as a seven year old,

00:04:15.024 --> 00:04:17.689
walking the streets of New Jersey sitting

00:04:17.689 --> 00:04:20.134
on corners watching cars drive by

00:04:20.134 --> 00:04:24.319
and trying to legitimately
figure out which tree,

00:04:24.319 --> 00:04:28.146
or which sign, or which
bush, or what angle

00:04:28.146 --> 00:04:31.282
their eyes were looking
at while they were driving

00:04:31.282 --> 00:04:33.255
and where to put my sign.

00:04:33.255 --> 00:04:37.046
I did not learn that in
college, I did not learn that

00:04:37.046 --> 00:04:40.035
by watching a keynote video
on YouTube, I did not learn

00:04:40.035 --> 00:04:43.060
that reading a Seth Godin book.

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:46.370
You know, I learned it because
it was inherently in me

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:48.366
and then it transformed forever.

00:04:48.366 --> 00:04:50.884
I did baseball card shows when I was 13,

00:04:50.884 --> 00:04:54.717
making $4,000 a weekend,
I was the only dealer

00:04:55.708 --> 00:04:59.477
amongst grown men, to spend
the first four or five hours

00:04:59.477 --> 00:05:02.856
not setting up my table but
walking around and understanding

00:05:02.856 --> 00:05:05.181
where the attention was going.

00:05:05.181 --> 00:05:08.154
I would spend a lot of
time looking at my table

00:05:08.154 --> 00:05:09.968
and understanding where to put things,

00:05:09.968 --> 00:05:11.964
because I knew they'd be walking by fast

00:05:11.964 --> 00:05:14.688
and could I stop them
with a Ken Griffy Jr.

00:05:14.688 --> 00:05:16.987
or a Micheal Jordan whatever it was.

00:05:16.987 --> 00:05:20.672
I'd been chasing attention my whole life.

00:05:20.672 --> 00:05:23.419
That manifested when I
transitioned in to my Dad's

00:05:23.419 --> 00:05:26.908
liquor store business
and it really transformed

00:05:26.908 --> 00:05:28.515
because I stood behind
the register and I watched

00:05:28.515 --> 00:05:31.717
people walk through the
store, and the first impact

00:05:31.717 --> 00:05:33.982
I had on my Dad's business
was moving around things.

00:05:33.982 --> 00:05:36.398
I said, "Dad, when people first
walk in we should not have

00:05:36.398 --> 00:05:38.861
a huge display of $6 stuff, we should

00:05:38.861 --> 00:05:40.240
have a display of $12."

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:43.739
It was just, it came natural,
it continues to come natural.

00:05:43.739 --> 00:05:46.572
I have written more books than I've read.

00:05:46.572 --> 00:05:51.019
I consume almost no content
other than reading peoples

00:05:51.019 --> 00:05:54.137
comments to things that
are going on in the world.

00:05:54.137 --> 00:05:58.130
I know that Felix Hernandez
retired from baseball last night

00:05:58.130 --> 00:06:00.987
by sitting in the green room
right now reading 20 peoples

00:06:00.987 --> 00:06:02.487
comments about it.

00:06:04.132 --> 00:06:07.768
I only care about the end consumer.

00:06:07.768 --> 00:06:11.274
I only care about the potential customer,

00:06:11.274 --> 00:06:15.819
and I care about her and
his behaviors and attention.

00:06:15.819 --> 00:06:20.819
I do not care what's currently
working for you to get leads.

00:06:21.168 --> 00:06:24.797
I don't care what's currently
working for me to get leads.

00:06:24.797 --> 00:06:29.155
I'm always putting what's
working yesterday through massive

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:32.602
friction of is that behavior best today.

00:06:32.602 --> 00:06:35.291
I built my Dad's liquor store from a three

00:06:35.291 --> 00:06:38.978
to a 60 million dollar
business in five years,

00:06:38.978 --> 00:06:42.246
on the back of spending
every penny properly

00:06:42.246 --> 00:06:45.816
even though the data
showed me that direct mail,

00:06:45.816 --> 00:06:50.392
and newspapers, and radios
would work better than email

00:06:50.392 --> 00:06:52.318
and google search.

00:06:52.318 --> 00:06:56.067
It didn't matter what it was
showing me, what mattered was

00:06:56.067 --> 00:06:58.562
what were human beings doing right now.

00:06:58.562 --> 00:07:00.891
To be a person in this
room looking for leads

00:07:00.891 --> 00:07:04.003
and growing their business,
and to not think social media

00:07:04.003 --> 00:07:06.170
works is audacious at best

00:07:07.231 --> 00:07:09.739
and downright fucking stupid at worst.

00:07:09.739 --> 00:07:11.175
(audience laughing)

00:07:11.175 --> 00:07:13.938
Now I understand why people think that,

00:07:13.938 --> 00:07:17.614
because like anything in
life the ROI of something

00:07:17.614 --> 00:07:22.077
is completely predicated
on how good you are at it.

00:07:22.077 --> 00:07:26.935
The ROI of a basketball is a
billion dollars for LeBron,

00:07:26.935 --> 00:07:29.119
it's zero for me.

00:07:29.119 --> 00:07:29.984
(audience laughing)

00:07:29.984 --> 00:07:33.287
Just cause you ran $1,000
worth of Facebook ads

00:07:33.287 --> 00:07:36.770
